values ('a1c2d3e4-5f6a-4b71-8c01-1d2e3f4a5b61', 'abnormal-psychology-psychopathology', 'Abnormal Psychology / Psychopathology', 'This course examines the classification, causes, assessment, lived experience, and treatment of psychological disorders. Students learn major diagnostic categories, biopsychosocial and developmental models, evidence-based interventions, cultural and ethical considerations, and the limits of diagnosis. The course emphasizes humane, scientifically grounded reasoning and clear boundaries: students learn about diagnosis and care systems, but do not practice diagnosis outside supervised professional contexts.');

